intent_dialogue:
0 TURKEY -> RUSSIA: So, skags gone. What are your thougghts. Hit nor wth 2.what is the cute little flash above Nor? I'm grading papers so I'll check from time to time. We have time. What do you want to do with keil.I'M movingg pied to tus, tri to ven. Supt tri to ven so I can go after Nap? I'm open to ideas on this.
1 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: Tyrol can support whatever you want. One option you have to protect Kiel is for Mun to hit Ruhr to cut whatever ruhr is doing. Tyrol would then support Boh to Mun to cover Mun.

We have a variety of options. One is we go for Den (Kiel moves to Den with Balt anc Swedish support). We hold Kiel by having Mun hit Ruhr (requires Tyrol and Boh to combine into Mun). But I think we have to get Swed to Fin and Gob to Sweden. Baltic ensures Gob gets to Sweden but baltic could also protect you in Kiel.

I have to look it over more.

Are you taking Bulg this turn? Either way, I assume I just hold in Bulg?
2 TURKEY -> RUSSIA: Not takeing Bulg this turn. You move out next turn, I take and we kill the fleet.
3 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: Sorry. It's been a busy couple days and didn't have a chance to look at this last night. I'm inclined to play it safe this turn and to work to set you up in the South. Tyrol will support Tri to Ven to ensure you get there. Getting rid of Italy is priority 1 for me since France-germany probably have me bottled up in the north. Not that I won't try, but you should be able to breakthrough in the south for sure. If we move at a good pace.
4 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: ugh, well on second thought. let me know what you want. I think they go for Kiel. In which case, Mun should hit Ruhr. And if Mun is moving, I'd like to use Tyrol to support Boh to Mun to ensure they don't take it.

So the question to you is do you want me to hit ruhr or use Tyrol to support Tri to Ven?

Do you want Baltic to support Kiel or to support Gob to Sweden?
5 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: Sorry to be so scatter brained. Here's what I'm thinking:

We win the game (or make them lose) by getting you through the south. So, I'm thinking about how best to accomplish that while taking some minor chances in the north.

Tyrol moves to Pie (to keep Mar out or to take it b/c why not?);
Mun hits Ruhr;
Boh moves to Mun;
War to Sil;
Ber support holds Kiel;
Baltic hits Den;
Sweden moves to Fin;
Both to Sweden;
St Petes supports Bar to Nor;
Bar to Nor; and
Rum holds (right?)

The reason to have Baltic hit Den is we don't know what it is doing. This ensures it can't support anything having to do with Kiel or Sweden. If it's moving, so be it. Mun will cut whatever Ruhr is doing against Kiel if it is helping or moving against Kiel. I take a chance on Mun getting blown up. And we take a chance therefore on losing Kiel the following turn if I lose Mun. Do we also take a chance wtih you getting to Ven? If so, I think it is worth it to keep mar out of Pie AND to keep mar in Mar so he can't build any fleets there. We at least complicate the situation in Mar for France. Realize this is a departure from me saying I didn't want to get stuck in Pie, but it makes sense to maximize the fall of Italy for you. the gains in the north limited for them while the potential losses by you busting through are quite huge.
6 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: One change. First turn I'm having St Pete support hold Bar Sea. It's possible France could nuke F Bar sea by having Nor support Nor Sea to Bar and nth sea support holding Nor. I need to setup first and I'm fairly certain that Nor isn't attainable right now anyway. the chance I take here is Nor could be supporting Den to Sweden. But that is highly unlikely I think.
7 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: have to run right now. not for sure that I get back online before the deadline:

my moves as of right now:

Mun to Ruhr;
Ber holds Kiel;
War to Sil;
Tyrol to Pie;
Boh to Mun;
Baltic to Den;
Swed to Fin;
Both to Swed;
St Pete holds Bar;
Bar holds;
rum holds.

If you want me to change anything, say so, but be prepared for me to be late. Think I'll have time to amend my moves if you want.
8 RUSSIA -> TURKEY: I'm finalizing to make it look less likely to France that I'm working with you. I've been talking with him and supposedly he is moving Ruhr to Bel. I doubt he will, but we shall see.
